{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy unit conversion from power and time energy unit conversion from power and time","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","fileName":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Power Rate Unit Conversion","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy unit conversion from power and time energy unit conversion from power and time","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","fileName":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time","heading":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Energy can be expressed as power accumulated over time. Pryor converts kilowatt-hours to joules by changing kilowatts to watts and hours to seconds, leaving watt-seconds, which equal joules. The factor chain produces $3.6\\times10^6\\ \\mathrm{J}$ for one kW·h. This illustrates why a time-bearing energy unit is not converted with a power factor alone. The book also lists other energy, work, and heat units in the same category. See [[Power Rate Unit Conversion]] and [[Conversion-Factor Chains]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Power Rate Unit Conversion","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy unit conversion from power and time energy unit conversion from power and time","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","fileName":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Unit Conversion from Power and Time","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Power Rate Unit Conversion","Conversion-Factor Chains","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}